            <profile id="4212-e6b9-eb64-34d5" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">All have thrusting spear and shield. May have large shield (+1) and be Riding Camels (+1). All may use a Combined Formation where up to half the figures in the unit exchange thrusting spear for composite bow (free) and form the rear ranks. Abid’ or Guards may have light armour (+2) and be Stubborn (+3). You may have up to one Abid’ or Guards unit per every two other infantry units.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="e255-7c0b-9234-02b2" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
